| R2 | MED check | User-fn arg cap types not enforced: `fn f(sys: &SysCap)` called with `&ProcessCap` / `&HttpCap` still **check OK**; sealed op inside `f` may pass if param is typed SysCap. Runtime token still fail-closed on require. | Broader TC/argflow residual; not process.oo signature. |
| R3 | LOW smoke | `sys_syscall_path_a_smoke` / `libfloor_process_smoke` forge sed zeros ambient `sys = grant` then main reassigns `sys = oo_cap_grant_sys()` — false "forge not denied". Require path itself not fail-open. | Smoke harness residual; R1 also breaks residual greps. |
| R4 | residual | Domain `std/async.oo` / `python.oo` still SysCap; ProcessCap std outside product `process.oo` incomplete. | CAP-G6/G7 residual named in CAPS. |

