No push.

========================================================================
PLAIN ENGLISH
========================================================================

What we proved:
1. A program that only has the **process** token may call **run a command** (check allows).
2. That same process-only token may **not** call **prctl** (check denies).
3. The full **system** token may call prctl (check allows).
4. The full system token may still call run-a-command (legacy supersede works).

The product wrapper file already asks for the small process token for run/spawn and keeps the big system token only for hard OS leftovers (prctl/epoll). No signature fix was needed.

What is still broken (named residual): the compiler’s C output currently mangles letter “r” in strings, so **running** process_exec on this host can fail even when check is green. That is an emit bug, not a wrong capability on the facade.
